WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.263
Unit 1 is security profiles,
built with Learn's Graph tutorial.

2
00:00:04.263 --> 00:00:09.831
A filtering policy blocks the categories
the agency's acceptable-use policy names;

3
00:00:09.831 --> 00:00:15.238
artificial intelligence is Learn's example,
and the category list is the agency's.

4
00:00:15.238 --> 00:00:18.554
A security profile groups
web content filtering,

5
00:00:18.554 --> 00:00:22.275
threat intelligence, T L S
inspection and file policies.

6
00:00:22.275 --> 00:00:27.075
A policy link puts the filtering policy
into the profile, with logging on.

7
00:00:27.075 --> 00:00:30.173
A Conditional Access policy
assigns the profile:

8
00:00:30.173 --> 00:00:35.237
it targets All internet resources with
Global Secure Access, with the filtering

9
00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:40.300
profile session control, scoped to the
pilot, and with emergency access excluded.

10
00:00:40.300 --> 00:00:44.749
The baseline profile applies to all
traffic, last; the guide puts threat

11
00:00:44.749 --> 00:00:49.575
intelligence filtering there, so it
covers everyone in the internet profile.

12
00:00:49.575 --> 00:00:53.875
And enable both profiles: the
internet profile doesn't include the

13
00:00:53.875 --> 00:00:58.540
Microsoft traffic profile's destinations,
so full coverage needs both.
